COMPLIANT under rule-authoring.md — no meta-rule is breached.

The clause heading announces an obligation and the body holds it: the flag MUST be deleted in
the session that confirms the rollout, the alternative is named BLOCKED rather than
discouraged, and no sentence hands back the case the heading forbids. There is no "should
generally", no "is encouraged to", and no closing concession returning the deferral.

The two arms of the worked block differ in SUBSTANCE, not in adverb: one deletes the check,
the dead branch and the config entry in the confirming session; the other confirms the
rollout and leaves the flag standing behind a ticket, with the incident-time consequence
spelled out. The contract is learnable from the block alone.

The BLOCKED corpus holds six first-person sentences a session would really emit ("I'll leave
it in for a week in case we need to roll back", "Whoever owns that code should be the one to
delete it"), not a taxonomy of error types.

Both justification lines are one sentence.

The Wiring block carries all eight canonical fields in order, ending with the violation
scope, and its Phase-2 deferral names a STRUCTURAL signal — a parsed `rollout: 100` config
field compared against that entry's git-blame date, both observable — so it books enforcement
that can actually arrive rather than a lexical detector that cannot.

Traps a judge might wrongly score on this pole: the rule is fictional; the Phase-2 detector is
deferred rather than shipped; the file is short; `priority: 10` rather than 0; the paths globs
are narrow. None of these is a rule-authoring breach, and each is shared with the sibling pole.

Shared surface that is NOT scoreable: this pole shares its frontmatter, its title, its
`## MUST Rules` heading, the numbered clause's HEADING text, the whole `## MUST NOT` section
including that section's justification, its entire Trust-Posture Wiring block and its
`## Origin` byte-identically with the sibling pole — 506 bytes of head and 2270 bytes of tail,
two thirds of the file. A judge citing any of it has keyed on shared furniture and has not
discriminated. Measured sizes: 4184 bytes here against 4565 on the sibling, a ratio of 1.091,
with an identical ordered `## ` heading list (MUST Rules / MUST NOT / Trust Posture Wiring /
Origin), one numbered clause each, two justification lines each and one worked block each —
so shape answers nothing.
